<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daewoo Motor union delays strike decision.</title>
<headline>Daewoo Motor union delays strike decision.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The union at South Korea's Daewoo Motor, a unit of the Daewoo Group, will put off a decision on strike action until after its leaders meet at 5.00 p.m. (0800 GMT) on Thursaday, a union official said.</p>
<p>&quot;The situation now is that work is going on as normal,&quot; said the official, who declined to be named.</p>
<p>He said union leaders would decided whether to recommend strike action to rank and file members, who would vote on Friday at 5.00 a.m. (2200 GMT Thursday).</p>
</text>
